<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vilshofen an der Donau</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Vilshofen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vilshofen an der Donau is a town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/passau">Passau</a> district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-bavaria">Lower Bavaria</a>, where the Vils joins the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> about 20 km upstream from Passau. Granted town rights in the early 13th century, it passed to the Wittelsbach dukes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> and lived from river trade. The castle of Ortenburg, seat of the counts of Ortenburg, lies in the hills to the south.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vilshofen-an-der-donau.jpg" alt="Vilshofen an der Donau" width="320" height="256" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Photographer: High Contrast; Perspective correction by Richard Bartz · CC BY 2.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vilshofen_an_der_Donau,_Vilsbr%C3%BCcke.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
